  "notes": [
    "The sequence is a shared counter that advances with the flywheel stroke, not a per-command or per-response counter. Several commands of one 1/2/3/4 cycle normally carry the same value.",
    "One command can legitimately return the same sequence twice in a row. Per-command sequences are non-decreasing but not strictly increasing.",
    "The global sequence stream is not monotonic: command 3 lags and produces six apparent decreases relative to the previous record.",
    "The device pads the sequence line with trailing spaces on some responses. The line is otherwise a plain unsigned decimal; nothing else in the capture carries padding.",
    "No reset command and no reset acknowledgement appear anywhere in this capture. The OK acknowledgement implemented by FitBridge comes from the E2 4.2.0 application analysis, not from this transcript.",
    "Arrival timestamps were not captured. Any replay must synthesize them and must not treat the synthesized cadence as observed."
